  "notes": "Crisis sites (Plans 5b and 6): each villain in villains.json has three lead sites (henchmen and the investigation; act I's is where the plan is learned) and three key sites (the prevention, against the act's boss). They are weight 0, so never drawn as ordinary POIs; the Crisis places them when it is rolled (and with them the villain's act biomes and seat hints). Category quest, never hostile: they don't feed threat or cycle. Their names are in crisis-names.json and their situations in crisis-situations.json. Every crisis site has water (an abandoned well, a spring or a cistern), so a party needs to carry water only for the way there: some sites lie 3–4 days off the road in the desert (Plan 5b I2; see docs/notes/crisis-report.md). Written by Claude; the act II and III leads were added in Plan 6 Track K.",
